//? Title: Planar and Radial Flows: Inverses, Volumes and Two Preserved Fits
//? Subtitle: Rank-one tanh changes and centre-based expansion on an analytic banana density
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A density model must track how a learned coordinate change expands or contracts
local area, while still recovering observations from latent draws. Planar and
radial flows make those calculations small: one changes points along a learned
direction, the other changes their distance from a centre. This native C++ study
starts with hand-checkable maps, then preserves both original four-stage fits,
strong-contraction fixtures, inverse parameter gradients and all 1,024 samples
per family. Fixed-final test NLL is 2.991511106 for planar and 2.999574184 for
radial, versus 2.994631823 for a fitting-only full Gaussian and 2.796480843 for
analytic truth. The radial fit falls short of that Gaussian baseline. These
short two-dimensional experiments reproduce the source; they do not establish
performance across seeds or on full-image density tasks.
)
\toc

> Two ways to make a tractable local volume change

[Rezende and Mohamed, Variational Inference with Normalizing Flows
(2015)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1505.05770) introduces planar and radial flow
families. Here they are standalone exact-density models, with no VAE or ELBO
workflow. Each family applies four elementary maps and a positive diagonal
scale, transforming observations x into standard-Gaussian coordinates z:

$$ \log p_X(x)=-\log(2\pi)-\tfrac12\|z\|^2+
\sum_{i=0}^3\log\det J_i(x_i)+\sum_{c=0}^1\mathrm{log\_scale}_c. $$
\alttext(The observation log density equals Gaussian latent log density plus four elementary-map log determinants and the final diagonal-scale log determinant.)

The fitting objective is negative mean log density, in nats per two-coordinate
row. Sampling starts with a supplied Gaussian z, removes the global scale, then
reverses stages 3,2,1,0. Each inverse log determinant is evaluated along its own
supplied path, rather than copied from a previous forward batch.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pr_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
