> Derive the planar determinant and numerical inverse

Let d=(cos a,sin a), e=exp(f), p=softplus(raw_projection)−.9, and
u=(p/e)d+q(−sin a,cos a), w=ed. Thus wᵀu=p>−.9>−1. The map is

$$ y=x+u\tanh(t),\quad t=w^Tx+b,\quad
J=I+u w^T(1-\tanh^2t),\quad
\det J=1+p(1-\tanh^2t)>0. $$
\alttext(The planar map adds a direction-weighted tanh. The rank-one determinant lemma reduces its Jacobian determinant to one plus projection times the tanh derivative.)

The rank-one determinant lemma gives the last equality. To invert y, form
c=wᵀy+b; the unknown t solves t+p tanh(t)=c. Its derivative is the positive
factor above, so there is one root. Since |p tanh(t)|<=|p|, c±(|p|+1)
brackets it. The source runs 32 bisections, then one Newton correction with
stopped root r and stopped denominator D=1+p(1−tanh²r):

$$ \hat t=r+\frac{(c-r)-p\tanh(r)}{D},\qquad
x=y-u\tanh(\hat t),\qquad d\hat t=\frac{dc-\tanh(r)\,dp}{D}. $$
\alttext(The numerical inverse refines a stopped bisection root with one Newton correction. Its first differential uses the implicit scalar equation while the denominator stays stopped.)

This is a numerical inverse. First derivatives follow the source implicit
correction without differentiating discrete bisection branches. Higher graphs
remain live through that correction, but their values follow the stopped root
and denominator; they are not exact higher implicit derivatives. Finite root
and floating-point residuals remain.

For a small worked map choose a=f=b=0, p=.5 and q=.25. Then
 y0=x0+.5 tanh(x0), y1=x1+.25 tanh(x0), det J=1+.5 sech²(x0).
At the origin, (0,0) stays fixed, J=[[1.5,0],[.25,1]], det J=1.5.
On the x1=0 slice, the first panel shows both changed coordinates and the
second shows the actual determinant. All five checked points and 257 native
curve evaluations are retained; no fitting data enter this example.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pr_planar_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;auto type=n::DType::Float64;
 auto scalar=[&](double v){return n::full({},v,type);};auto zero=scalar(0),raw=scalar(std::log(std::expm1(1.4))),q=scalar(.25);
 auto axis=n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{-2,-1,0,1,2},{5});auto x=n::stack({axis,n::zeros({5},type)},1).requires_grad_();
 auto f=m::PlanarFlow(x,zero,zero,raw,q,zero),rec=m::PlanarFlow(f.value,zero,zero,raw,q,zero,true);
 auto keep=n::GradOptions{true,false,false};auto j0=n::grad(n::sum(n::slice_axis(f.value,1,0,1)),{x},keep)[0],j1=n::grad(n::sum(n::slice_axis(f.value,1,1,2)),{x},keep)[0];
 auto det=n::select(j0,1,0)*n::select(j1,1,1)-n::select(j0,1,1)*n::select(j1,1,0);
 auto wanted=n::stack({axis+.5*n::tanh(axis),.25*n::tanh(axis)},1),wanted_det=1.+.5*(1.-n::square(n::tanh(axis)));
 if(n::max(n::abs(f.value-wanted)).item()>1e-14||n::max(n::abs(det-wanted_det)).item()>1e-14||n::max(n::abs(rec.value-x)).item()>1e-14||n::max(n::abs(n::log(det)-f.logdet)).item()>1e-14)throw std::runtime_error("Worked planar map");
 auto dense=n::arange(0,257,1,type)/64.-2.;auto curve_input=n::stack({dense,n::zeros({257},type)},1).requires_grad_();auto curve=m::PlanarFlow(curve_input,zero,zero,raw,q,zero);
 auto a=n::grad(n::sum(n::slice_axis(curve.value,1,0,1)),{curve_input},keep)[0],b=n::grad(n::sum(n::slice_axis(curve.value,1,1,2)),{curve_input},keep)[0];
 auto curve_det=n::select(a,1,0)*n::select(b,1,1)-n::select(a,1,1)*n::select(b,1,0);
 auto left=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
 left.lines(dense.to_vector<double>(),n::select(curve.value,1,0).to_vector<double>(),"y0 = x0 + .5 tanh(x0)",{37,99,235})
 .lines(dense.to_vector<double>(),n::select(curve.value,1,1).to_vector<double>(),"y1 = .25 tanh(x0)",{234,88,12})
 .points(axis.to_vector<double>(),n::select(f.value,1,0).to_vector<double>(),"Five y0 checks",{37,99,235},4)
 .points(axis.to_vector<double>(),n::select(f.value,1,1).to_vector<double>(),"Five y1 checks",{234,88,12},4)
 .margins(78,22,54,70).x_limits(-2.3,2.3).y_limits(-2.8,5).x_label("Input x0, x1=0").y_label("Output coordinate").title("Planar: rank-one tanh change");
 auto right=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();right.lines(dense.to_vector<double>(),curve_det.to_vector<double>(),"Actual determinant",{37,99,235})
 .lines({-2,2},{1,1},"Identity area factor",{148,163,184})
 .points(axis.to_vector<double>(),det.to_vector<double>(),"Five actual checks",{220,38,38},4)
 .margins(78,22,54,70).x_limits(-2.3,2.3).y_limits(.9,2.2).x_label("Input x0").y_label("Positive area factor").title("det J = 1 + .5 sech^2(x0)");
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(left).add(right).size(1100,520).fit_panels().save_svg("build/pr_planar_toy.svg");
 n::save_npz("build/pr_planar_toy_values.npz",{{"axis",axis},{"input",x},{"value",f.value},{"logdet",f.logdet},{"actual_determinant",det},{"recovered",rec.value},{"inverse_logdet",rec.logdet},{"dense_axis",dense},{"curve",curve.value},{"curve_determinant",curve_det}});
 std::print("| x0 | y0 | y1 | Actual determinant |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");auto a0=axis.to_vector<double>(),v=f.value.to_vector<double>(),dv=det.to_vector<double>();
 for(int i=0;i<5;++i)std::print("|{:.1f}|{:.10f}|{:.10f}|{:.10f}|\n",a0[i],v[2*i],v[2*i+1],dv[i]);
}
