> Derive radial tangential and radial factors

With centre c, r=||x−c||, alpha=.1+softplus(raw_alpha)>0 and
beta=softplus(raw_beta)−alpha>−alpha, write

$$ y=c+g(r)(x-c),\quad g(r)=1+\frac{\beta}{\alpha+r},\quad
\det J=\left(1+\frac{\beta}{\alpha+r}\right)
\left(1+\frac{\beta\alpha}{(\alpha+r)^2}\right)>0. $$
\alttext(The radial map rescales each centred vector. Its two-dimensional determinant is the product of its tangential and radial eigenvalue factors.)

For r>0, the tangential eigenvalue is g(r); the radial one is
g(r)+r g'(r)=1+beta alpha/(alpha+r)². Both stay positive under beta>−alpha.
At the centre, the value Jacobian is (1+beta/alpha)I. The source selects a
zero radius derivative there, including its chosen logdet partial; it does not
claim a smooth mathematical Hessian of radius or logdet at the centre. Tiny
positive squared radii use sqrt(max(square,1e−30)), preserving the source rule.

For an inverse input distance rho=||y−c||, the source radius solves
r²+(alpha+beta−rho)r−alpha rho=0. Let a=alpha+beta−rho and
s=sqrt(a²+4 alpha rho). Use 2 alpha rho/(a+s) when a>=0, or (s−a)/2
otherwise, with a stabilized inactive denominator. This avoids cancellation in
the positive root. Recover x=c+(y−c)/g(r) and negate the forward log determinant
at recovered r. Both branches are retained.

Choose c=0, alpha=1 and beta=1 for a worked expansion. Radii 0,.5,1,2 map to
0,5/6,1.5,8/3. The origin has value Jacobian 2I and area factor 4. The curves
below retain 257 native evaluations; all four rational-radius checks, their
actual two-dimensional determinants and stable inverses are checked.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pr_radial_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;auto type=n::DType::Float64;
 auto center=n::zeros({2},type),alpha=n::full({},std::log(std::expm1(.9)),type),beta=n::full({},std::log(std::expm1(2.)),type);
 auto axis=n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{0,.5,1,2},{4});auto x=n::stack({axis,n::zeros({4},type)},1).requires_grad_();
 auto f=m::RadialFlow(x,center,alpha,beta),rec=m::RadialFlow(f.value,center,alpha,beta,true);auto keep=n::GradOptions{true,false,false};
 auto j0=n::grad(n::sum(n::slice_axis(f.value,1,0,1)),{x},keep)[0],j1=n::grad(n::sum(n::slice_axis(f.value,1,1,2)),{x},keep)[0];
 auto det=n::select(j0,1,0)*n::select(j1,1,1)-n::select(j0,1,1)*n::select(j1,1,0),wanted=n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{0,5./6.,1.5,8./3.},{4});
 auto wanted_det=(1.+1./(1.+axis))*(1.+1./n::square(1.+axis));
 if(n::max(n::abs(n::select(f.value,1,0)-wanted)).item()>1e-14||n::max(n::abs(det-wanted_det)).item()>1e-14||n::max(n::abs(rec.value-x)).item()>1e-14||n::max(n::abs(n::log(det)-f.logdet)).item()>1e-14)throw std::runtime_error("Worked radial map");
 auto dense=n::arange(0,257,1,type)/128.;auto grid=n::stack({dense,n::zeros({257},type)},1).requires_grad_();auto curve=m::RadialFlow(grid,center,alpha,beta);
 auto a=n::grad(n::sum(n::slice_axis(curve.value,1,0,1)),{grid},keep)[0],b=n::grad(n::sum(n::slice_axis(curve.value,1,1,2)),{grid},keep)[0];
 auto curve_det=n::select(a,1,0)*n::select(b,1,1)-n::select(a,1,1)*n::select(b,1,0);
 auto left=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();left.lines(dense.to_vector<double>(),n::select(curve.value,1,0).to_vector<double>(),"Native output radius",{37,99,235})
 .lines({0,2},{0,2},"Identity radius",{148,163,184}).points(axis.to_vector<double>(),wanted.to_vector<double>(),"Four rational checks",{220,38,38},4)
 .margins(78,22,54,70).x_limits(-.1,2.1).y_limits(-.1,4.2).x_label("Input radius r").y_label("Output radius").title("Radial: r maps to r + r/(1+r)");
 auto right=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();right.lines(dense.to_vector<double>(),curve_det.to_vector<double>(),"Actual determinant",{37,99,235})
 .lines({0,2},{1,1},"Identity area factor",{148,163,184}).points(axis.to_vector<double>(),det.to_vector<double>(),"Four actual checks",{220,38,38},4)
 .margins(78,22,54,70).x_limits(-.1,2.1).y_limits(.8,6.2).x_label("Input radius r").y_label("Positive area factor").title("Tangential times radial factor");
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(left).add(right).size(1100,520).fit_panels().save_svg("build/pr_radial_toy.svg");
 n::save_npz("build/pr_radial_toy_values.npz",{{"axis",axis},{"input",x},{"value",f.value},{"actual_determinant",det},{"logdet",f.logdet},{"recovered",rec.value},{"inverse_logdet",rec.logdet},{"dense_axis",dense},{"curve",curve.value},{"curve_determinant",curve_det}});
 std::print("| Input radius | Output radius | Actual determinant |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n");auto xv=axis.to_vector<double>(),yv=n::select(f.value,1,0).to_vector<double>(),dv=det.to_vector<double>();
 for(int i=0;i<4;++i)std::print("|{:.1f}|{:.10f}|{:.10f}|\n",xv[i],yv[i],dv[i]);
}
