> Trace both independently parameterized four-stage models

Each planar block owns five scalar leaves: angle, log_frequency, raw_projection,
perpendicular and bias. Source angles use Float32 arithmetic .4f+.65f*block
before promotion; alternating perpendicular values use .02f and −.02f.
The other initial values are 0,.4,.05 respectively. Four blocks plus global
log_scale[2] give **22 values in 21 leaves**. Each radial block owns centre[2]
initialized normal(.2), raw_alpha=.4 and raw_beta=.56: four values in three
leaves. Four plus the global two give **18 values in 13 leaves**.

Both separate stores use seed 9903. Warm forward blocks 0..3 then global scale
to retain source initialization order; the optional reference initialization
arrays are absent. The following diagrams execute the selected native family
and group two blocks per stage: planar 10+10+2 values, radial 8+8+2. Public
factor/coordinate fields have family-specific meanings; the old source archives
call them coupling_scale/coupling_shift. These are diagnostics, not affine log
scales or shifts.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pr_planar_network.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore p(9903);
 n::Module model([&](const n::Tensor& x){auto o=n::models::PlanarRadialDensity(p,x,false);
  n::model_stage("Planar stages 0 / 1",x,o.flow1);
  n::model_stage("Planar stages 2 / 3",o.flow1,o.unscaled);
  return n::model_stage("Positive diagonal scale",o.unscaled,o.latent);
 },"Planar: 22 values / 21 leaves");
 n::ModelPlotOptions options;options.detail=n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;options.sizing.minimum_extent=2;options.sizing.max_planes=2;
 auto figure=model.plot(n::zeros({1,2}),options);
 if(figure.parameter_count()!=22||p.size()!=21)throw std::runtime_error("Executed Planar census");
 figure.save_svg("build/pr_planar_network.svg");
}
