// result_end

> Inspect the original strong-contraction fixtures

Each family keeps all nine original points, including the declared planar hinge
and the exact radial centre (.3f,−.2f). Planar fixture parameters are angle .6f,
log_frequency .3f, raw_projection −6f, perpendicular .7f and bias .1f; its hinge
coordinates are formed with the source Double trigonometry then cast to Float32.
The radial fixture uses raw_alpha .4f and raw_beta=Float32(log(expm1(.12))),
so alpha+beta is near .12 and the centre contracts strongly. These are fixed
fixture parameters, distinct from the fitted models.

In each first panel grey segments connect supplied points to forward values;
all nine inputs, forward outputs and inverses of those same supplied inputs are
retained. Inverse points are not roundtrips. The second panel retains all nine
analytic and actual determinants in both directions. The tables retain all
coordinates, both log determinants and roundtrip errors. Source checks allow
2e−5 on strong-contraction roundtrip and forward actual/logdet differences;
the displayed Float32 residuals are smaller. The radial centre value Jacobians
are finite factor*I and I/factor; source radius/logdet centre partials use zero.

