> Retain every observation and the fixed-final outcomes

The common observation plot retains all 768 original rows. The two three-epoch
validation paths are descriptive: both final checkpoints were fixed in advance.
The comparison table uses the same held-out rows and fitting-only Gaussian
moments for both families. Planar improves only slightly on the full Gaussian;
radial finishes worse. Both remain above analytic truth. No between-run
uncertainty or broad generalization improvement is claimed.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pr_data.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> data;
 for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/planar_radial_density/planar/data.npz"))data[key]=value;
 auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();int i=0;
 std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors{{148,163,184},{37,99,235},{234,88,12}};
 for(auto split:{"fit","validation","test"}){auto points=data.at(std::string(split)+"_points");
  plot.points(n::select(points,1,0).to_vector<double>(),n::select(points,1,1).to_vector<double>(),split,colors[i++],3);}
 plot.size(900,942).margins(90,24,72,84).x_limits(-4,7).y_limits(-4,7)
 .x_label("x0").y_label("x1").title("Original banana pools: every row retained")
 .save_svg("build/pr_data.svg");
}
