> Interpret the density and derivative checks together

For every supplied prior draw, the log identity is
log p_X(inverse(z))+log|det J_inverse(z)|=log phi(z). The residuals above check
that identity numerically on every sample. They do not claim an independently
computed global density integral. Both forward/inverse coordinate roundtrips
have source maximum errors 4.768371582e−7. Fixed-final likelihood evidence is
mixed: the planar model is only .003120717 nats/row below the full Gaussian,
while radial is .004942361 above it. Both remain well above analytic truth.

The source is preserved at its original scope: separate tiny two-dimensional
models, three fixed epochs, one initialization per family and procedural banana
observations. No additional fit, seed search, test-based selection or VAE/ELBO
claim is introduced. The editable program and core APIs retain all 48 original
archives / 281,879 array values and all 288 update captures / 3,936 values
exactly, including both strong fixtures and every inverse parameter gradient.
Independent NumPy calculations use explicit elementary differentials and matrix
composition, with no native-helper calls, external autodiff, refit or substitute
data. The report exposes the numerical planar inverse and derivative caveat,
radial centre convention and the radial Gaussian shortfall alongside the plots.

